## 2. Content Rule (read first)

Nothing about the firm may be stated as fact unless the client confirmed it.

- All copy that depends on the client lives in `src/data/content.ts`, with bracketed placeholders such as `[Project Name]`, `[Typology · City · Year]`, `[X]`, `[Principal Name]`.
- Stats, client logos, testimonials, certifications and capability claims stay as placeholders, or are hidden, until verified.
- Stats (`[X] Projects · [X] Years · [X] Cities`) in the About section are **hidden** until the client has numbers that look credible. A small number shown as a stat hurts more than no stat.
- The layout reference site's copy, numbers, claims (homeowner counts, handover times, warranties), imagery, logo and testimonials are never reused. Slide headlines come from this spec or from the client.
- Sustainability or carbon claims are not allowed without a documented source from the client.
- The "Design + Make" columns stay as `[What we fabricate 1–3]` until the client confirms what they manufacture.
- Portfolio destination URLs live in `content.ts` as `[Architecture Portfolio URL]` and `[Interiors Portfolio URL]`. Do not link anywhere unconfirmed. If a URL is still a placeholder at launch, the link is hidden, not left broken.

