## 4. Page Structure (top to bottom)

Layout reference: the home page of https://www.rakinteriors.com/. Only the structure and section order are followed. Fab Haus keeps its own colors, fonts, copy rules and single-page format.

1. **Utility bar** (thin strip above the header)
   - Left: `[Email]` and `[Phone]`. Background `--color-surface`.
   - Scrolls away with the page. Hidden below 768px (the same details appear in Contact and the footer).
2. **Header** (sticky)
   - Left: wordmark `FAB HAUS`. Right: `Home`, `About`, `Work` (dropdown: `Architecture ↗`, `Interiors ↗`, both external, new tab), `Design + Make`, `Process`, and a primary `Get in touch` button.
   - Always visible. Transparent over the hero with a subtle dark backing, solid `--color-bg` with a hairline border after 80px of scroll.
   - Active section link is highlighted.
   - Mobile: menu button opens a drawer. The `Work` dropdown becomes an accordion inside it.
3. **Hero slider** (full-bleed, `min(100svh, 900px)`)
   - Three slides, each with a full-bleed image under a dark overlay (at least 40%), a very large headline, a small uppercase label (`[Slide label]`), one tagline line (`[Slide tagline]`) and one button:
     - Slide 1: "Designed. Built. Delivered." → `View our work` (anchors to Work).
     - Slide 2: "From drawing to built, under one roof." → `Explore Design + Make`.
     - Slide 3: "Let's build something real." → `Get in touch`.
   - Controls: previous/next arrows, dots, swipe on touch, and a visible pause/play button.
   - Stat-led slides are allowed only once the client supplies verified figures (section 2).
4. **About** (light section, two columns)
   - Left: heading, `[Firm statement]`, short story `[About paragraph]`, optional founder quote `"[Principal quote]"` — `[Principal Name]`.
   - Right: image `[About Image]`.
   - Optional stats row (`[X] Projects · [X] Years · [X] Cities`), hidden until real figures are supplied.
5. **Drawing to Built** (before/after compare)
   - A drag slider comparing a render or drawing with a photo of the same project (`[Render Image]`, `[Built Image]`), with a caption `[Project Name]`.
   - Hidden if the client has no matching pair.
6. **What We Do** (two segment cards)
   - Two cards side by side (stacked on mobile): `Architecture` and `Interiors`. Each has an image, the title, `[Category description]` and a link `View architecture work ↗` / `View interior work ↗`.
   - Links open the full portfolio in a new tab (see section 6).
7. **Design + Make** (the differentiator)
   - Two images side by side: architecture (drawing or render) and fabrication (workshop or material close-up).
   - Heading: "From drawing to built, under one roof."
   - Three short columns: `[What we fabricate 1]`, `[What we fabricate 2]`, `[What we fabricate 3]`.
8. **Process** (dark band)
   - Four steps in a row (stacked on mobile): `01 Discover`, `02 Design`, `03 Fabricate`, `04 Install`, each with a one-line description. Numerals in the accent color. Static, no pinning.
9. **Video** (optional)
   - `[Video URL]` shown as a poster with a play button. The embed loads only after the visitor clicks. Hidden if no video.
10. **Testimonials** (carousel, optional)
    - Cards with quote text, name and location (`[Testimonial]`, `[Client Name]`, `[Location]`), optional photo. Client logos (`[Client logos]`) may sit beneath. Hidden entirely if the client has none yet. Do not fake it.
11. **Contact** (dark, full-width)
    - Headline "Let's build something real."
    - `[Email]`, `[Phone]`, `[Address]`, plus a `mailto:` button and a WhatsApp button (`https://wa.me/<digits only, country code, no + or spaces>`). No form in Phase 1.
12. **Footer** (multi-column)
    - Columns: Quick links (page sections), Work (`Architecture ↗`, `Interiors ↗`), Contact (`[Address]`, `[Phone]`, `[Email]`).
    - `[Instagram]`, `[LinkedIn]` and other networks the client actually has. `[Download Brochure]` (PDF, new tab) only if supplied. Copyright line.
13. **Floating action buttons** (fixed, right edge)
    - Icon stack: WhatsApp, Call, and Instagram (only if the client has it), plus a fixed `Get in touch` tab that scrolls to Contact. It is a link, not a form.
    - 44px minimum tap targets, safe-area insets respected, must not cover content or form a trap on small screens.

**Fallbacks when assets are missing** (the client has little material)
- Hero: fewer than two supplied images means a single static slide with no controls or autoplay.
- About image missing: text-only, centered statement.
- Drawing to Built: no matching pair means the section is hidden.
- Segment card image missing: text-only card on `--color-surface`.
- Design + Make images missing: text columns only, no image pair.
- Video, testimonials, brochure and social links: hidden when absent.
- Mock only: a missing image renders as a neutral `--color-surface` block labelled with its placeholder name (for example `[Hero Image]`), so the client can see what is needed. At go-live the fallbacks above apply.

