## 11. Phase 2: Conversational Lead Qualifier (after launch)

**Goal:** separate serious enquiries from casual price-checkers, and explain prefab / light-gauge steel framing in plain language so clients do not back off at the jargon.

**Why it is a separate phase:** Phase 1 deliberately removed calculators and forms. This feature needs real client data (pricing ranges) that does not exist yet, and a small backend. It ships only after Phase 1 is live and the client data is supplied.

**Scope**
- A "Plan your project" button (in Contact and optionally the nav) opening a themed side or full-screen chat panel.
- Lazy-loaded on click so LCP and CLS budgets in section 6 still hold.
- No auto-popping chat bubble. It clashes with the slow, confident motion principles and annoys visitors.

**Rules**
- Questions use outcomes, never jargon. Examples: do you own a plot, when do you want to move in, would you prefer a faster factory-built home or a traditional on-site build.
- Technical terms are explained in one plain sentence only when relevant.
- Price output is always a **range labelled "indicative only"**. No exact quotes.
- Estimates use only client-supplied rate ranges. No invented figures (see Content Rule, section 2).
- Do not gate the first rough range behind a phone number. Ask for contact details after value is shown, to send a detailed breakdown.
- Scoring is **explicit rules**, not AI judgment, so it is predictable and tunable:
  - Land: owns a plot (strong), purchasing (medium), none (weak)
  - Timeline: under 6 months (hot), 12+ months (nurture)
  - Budget realism against the size described
  - Decision-maker: is the user the one deciding
  - Contact shared: yes or no
- Output: **Hot / Warm / Cold** plus a 3-line summary the owner can read in 10 seconds.
- Hot leads are delivered to the client's chosen channel (WhatsApp, email or CRM).

**Technical**
- A small serverless function (for example on Vercel) holds the API key and sends the lead summary. No key ever lives in the frontend.
- Chat UI uses the existing design tokens so it feels native to the site.

**Accessibility**
- Focus trap, `Esc` closes, focus returns to the trigger button, reduced-motion respected, same standard as the drawer menu.

**Needed from the client**
- Project types they take (villa, farmhouse, commercial, etc.) and rough cost-per-sq-ft ranges for each.
- What they will not take (minimum size, locations not served).
- What a good lead looks like to them, and how enquiries are handled today.
- Who receives leads and on which channel.

**Acceptance**
- [ ] No exact price shown anywhere.
- [ ] Every figure traceable to client-supplied data.
- [ ] Lead summary arrives on the chosen channel within seconds.
- [ ] Page performance budgets unchanged when the chat is closed.
- [ ] API key is not present in any frontend bundle.

